From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bayles <jophba@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] layer3: Allow block_type mismatch between channels in joint stereo

Currently, `stereo.rs` requires both channels in a joint stereo frame to
share the same `block_type`.

However, the MPEG-1 Layer 3 specification stores block types per channel
in the side information. Real-world encoders (such as Zoom H1n handheld
recorders and LAME) can select different window types for each channel
(e.g., using a short window for a transient on one channel while keeping
a long window on the other) even when using Mid-Side stereo.

Because Mid-Side stereo decorrelation simply operates on frequency bins
before each channel runs its own antialiasing, IMDCT, and windowing, the
channels' block types don't need to match. Removing this check allows
these bitstreams to decode without errors.
Upstream issue: https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia/issues/556
Upstream PR: https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia/pull/557
Chromium bug: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/563087658

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/symphonia-bundle-mp3-v0_6/src/layer3/stereo.rs b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/symphonia-bundle-mp3-v0_6/src/layer3/stereo.rs
index 65a747355321e..400ebcf6e2b7a 100644
--- a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/symphonia-bundle-mp3-v0_6/src/layer3/stereo.rs
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/symphonia-bundle-mp3-v0_6/src/layer3/stereo.rs
@@ -499,11 +499,6 @@ pub(super) fn stereo(
         _ => return Ok(()),
     };
 
-    // The block types must be the same.
-    if granule.channels[0].block_type != granule.channels[1].block_type {
-        return decode_error("mpa: stereo channel pair block_type mismatch");
-    }
-
     // Split the sample buffer into two channels.
     let (ch0, ch1) = {
         let (ch0, ch1) = match ch.split_first_mut() {
